{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_142908_388587", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Email 1: Subject \u2014 Reduce cloud workstation costs without losing capability\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour engineers rely on cloud-hosted workstations for CAD and simulation. That model works when connectivity is reliable and data stays in the office. It struggles on site visits and adds a recurring monthly cost to every seat.\n\nA mobile workstation that handles AI tasks locally can lower that cloud bill while keeping client data under your control. With on-device processing for language models up to 30 billion parameters, your team can work offline at construction sites or during travel.\n\nYou also get predictable hardware refresh cycles instead of ongoing subscription fees. Fewer device types simplify fleet management. Security features like TPM 2.0 and self-healing BIOS keep projects protected whether online or offline.\n\nYour budget cycle closes at the end of Q1. Approving pilot units now means deployment before the window shuts.\n\nCall to action: Reply with \"brief\" and I will send a one-page cost comparison.\n\n---\n\nEmail 2: Subject \u2014 Cloud-first teams use local power for offline work\n\nMorgan,\n\nCloud workstations handle heavy rendering well. They require stable internet and incur monthly fees per user. When engineers visit job sites with unreliable connectivity, productivity drops. Client drawings stay locked behind the firewall.\n\nThe Aurora 14 runs AI models locally without sending data to external servers. Its NPU delivers 60 TOPS for on-device inference. With 64 GB of memory or more, it handles open-weight language models up to about 30 billion parameters directly on the laptop.\n\nThis means engineers annotate client drawings, run simulations, and access project files offline. Data never leaves the device unless they choose to sync it. Your security posture improves because sensitive files don't transit public networks unnecessarily.\n\nMemory and storage are user-upgradeable through SO-DIMM and M.2 slots. You can configure units based on role requirements rather than buying top-tier specs for everyone.\n\nCall to action: Reply with \"specs\" and I will send configuration options for your engineer roles.\n\n---\n\nEmail 3: Subject \u2014 Schedule a 15-minute review before Q1 closes\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour budget cycle ends this quarter. Waiting until next year delays deployment by twelve months and locks in current cloud costs for another year.\n\nA brief meeting lets us review three items: total cost comparison between cloud-only and hybrid approaches, security controls that meet your firm's requirements, and a pilot program timeline that fits your Q1 approval window.\n\nI will bring facts only. No demos, no pressure. Just numbers and options you can take to your finance team.\n\nIf Q1 has already closed or you prefer to wait, say so and I will follow up in Q4 when availability opens.\n\nCall to action: Book a 15-minute slot here [insert calendar link] or reply with your preferred time.", "tokens": {"input": 4666, "output": 590, "total": 5256, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 14814, "timestamp": 1790803763669}